## SHARED FILES (one owner at a time; landings are serial)
- **`Datasec.Suite.slnx`: exactly your four lines, placed by `place.py <file> full` (THE TOOLS), nothing else in that file.** The rule (the lane plan's "The shared files" rule 1): inside its folder each line goes directly BEFORE the first existing project line whose Path is greater by ordinal comparison, else after the folder's last project line, against the file AS IT STANDS. **The numbers in THE TOOLS are main's at drafting: you print YOURS.**
- **`Directory.Packages.props`: exactly three lines, placed by `placeprops.py <file> <EF> <NPGSQL>` with the two versions of Stamp S4 (defaults `10.0.15` and `10.0.4`).** At main the file is 11 lines with 4 `PackageVersion` lines (`Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.WindowsServices` `[10.0.15]`, `Serilog` `[4.4.0]`, `Serilog.Sinks.File` `[7.0.0]`, `xunit.v3` `[4.0.3]`; MEASURED). Lane B is the only owner of this file in the wave (RELAYED, the wave-2 plan); a conflict in it at a rebase means another lane touched it: STOP.
